From fadafb1cd2afe2c9b506f7ef0c61e4085ebbd880 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julian Cooper <115541810+Juliansgith@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 15:12:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 02/56] Fold CScrLuaMetatableFactory specializations into the
 primary template

45 translation units declared their own explicit specialization of
CScrLuaMetatableFactory<T> (class body in the .cpp, out-of-line sInstance /
Instance / Create) while other translation units instantiated the primary
template for the same T. That is an ODR violation; with Release inlining,
callers ended up with two singletons per type, so Lua methods were registered
on one metatable while objects were created with the other and scripts saw
nil methods (Unit:SetBusy, GetWeaponCount, HideBone,
GetAirUnitsEmphasis, ...).

The primary template in CScrLuaObjectFactory.h already does the same thing
(function-local static instance, SCR_CreateSimpleMetatable), so the
specializations are removed and every translation unit shares one
definition.

(cherry picked from commit a7ed6b6499796c7f5c3824e89be67e2c981de6f2)

Ported onto 8977bb9d: kept upstream's new CLuaConOutputHandler::GetPointerType/sPointerType beside the removed sInstance.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
